  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{0}\\frac{1}{3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{3}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3+6 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
